Always use TypeScript in strict mode.
Always use Next.js App Router (not Pages Router).
Always use Tailwind CSS with the tokens defined in tailwind.config.ts —
never hardcode hex colors, always use the semantic token names
(accent, ink, paper, sidebar, success/danger/warning).
Always use Shadcn UI for base components (buttons, inputs, dialogs).
Use Zustand for lightweight global state, React Query for all API/data
fetching and caching.
Use React Hook Form with Zod for every form — never rely on native
browser validation.
This app is Arabic-first (RTL) with English as a secondary language (LTR)
via toggle. Default <html dir="rtl" lang="ar">. Use logical Tailwind
spacing (ms-/me-/ps-/pe-) instead of ml-/mr-/pl-/pr- everywhere, so layouts
mirror correctly when switching to English.
Follow the folder structure defined in frontend_architecture_guide-v2.md
exactly: app/(auth), app/(core), app/(plugins), components/ui,
components/layout, components/shared, lib/, store/, types/.
Wrap every route and every plugin component in an Error Boundary.
Use next/dynamic for lazy-loading any plugin screen or heavy component.
Never build a new <Table> or <Form> from scratch — always extend the
shared <DataTable /> component once it exists.
Numeric and currency figures always use font-mono and render LTR
(dir="ltr") even inside RTL layout.
Never duplicate the Sidebar or Navbar per screen — always import the
shared components/layout/Sidebar.tsx and components/layout/Navbar.tsx.
